          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For any ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\triangle ABC",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", Mollweide’s formulas state that:",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p11-q8-formulas-native",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "center",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a+b}{c}&=\\frac{\\cos\\left[\\frac12(A-B)\\right]}{\\cos\\left[\\frac12(A+B)\\right]},\\\\\\frac{a-b}{c}&=\\frac{\\sin\\left[\\frac12(A-B)\\right]}{\\sin\\left[\\frac12(A+B)\\right]}.\\end{aligned}",
              "display": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Using the sine rule, prove these formulas.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Both formulas follow from $\\dfrac{a}{c}=\\dfrac{\\sin A}{\\sin C}$ and $\\dfrac{b}{c}=\\dfrac{\\sin B}{\\sin C}$.\n\nApply the sum-to-product formulas and use $A+B=\\pi-C$.",
          "worked": "The sine rule gives $\\dfrac{a}{c}=\\dfrac{\\sin A}{\\sin C}$ and $\\dfrac{b}{c}=\\dfrac{\\sin B}{\\sin C}$. Also, $A+B=\\pi-C$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{a+b}{c}&=\\frac{\\sin A+\\sin B}{\\sin C}\\\\\\frac{a+b}{c}&=\\frac{2\\sin\\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)}{2\\sin\\frac C2\\cos\\frac C2}\\\\\\frac{a+b}{c}&=\\frac{\\cos\\frac C2\\cos\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)}{\\sin\\frac C2\\cos\\frac C2}\\\\\\frac{a+b}{c}&=\\frac{\\cos\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)}{\\sin\\frac C2}\\\\\\frac{a+b}{c}&=\\frac{\\cos\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)}{\\cos\\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right)}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{a-b}{c}&=\\frac{\\sin A-\\sin B}{\\sin C}\\\\\\frac{a-b}{c}&=\\frac{2\\cos\\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)}{2\\sin\\frac C2\\cos\\frac C2}\\\\\\frac{a-b}{c}&=\\frac{\\sin\\frac C2\\sin\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)}{\\sin\\frac C2\\cos\\frac C2}\\\\\\frac{a-b}{c}&=\\frac{\\sin\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)}{\\cos\\frac C2}\\\\\\frac{a-b}{c}&=\\frac{\\sin\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)}{\\sin\\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right)}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 132
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p11-q8-b-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Hence, prove that",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p11-q8-b-identity",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "center",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\frac{a+b}{a-b}=\\frac{\\tan\\left[\\frac12(A+B)\\right]}{\\tan\\left[\\frac12(A-B)\\right]}.",
                  "display": true
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p11-q8-b-name-native",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "This identity is known as the ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "tangent rule",
                  "marks": [
                    "bold"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ", or ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "law of tangents",
                  "marks": [
                    "bold"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{a+b}{a-b}=\\dfrac{\\tan\\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right)}{\\tan\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)}$.\n\nDivide the two Mollweide formulas.",
          "worked": "Divide the first Mollweide formula by the second, where the expressions are defined.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{a+b}{a-b}&=\\frac{(a+b)/c}{(a-b)/c}\\\\\\frac{a+b}{a-b}&=\\frac{\\cos\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)}{\\cos\\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right)}\\cdot\\frac{\\sin\\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right)}{\\sin\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)}\\\\\\frac{a+b}{a-b}&=\\frac{\\tan\\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right)}{\\tan\\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right)}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
